      "pitch": {
        "hook": "From private studio notes to a public artist presence that institutions can actually navigate.",
        "challenge": "Jieshin’s practice spans sculpture, installation, painting and writing between London and Taiwan — but the work lived as scattered folders, Instagram fragments and closed studio notes. For a degree-show year and residency cycle, that made the practice hard to brief, hard to cite, and hard to commission.",
        "influence": "The website positions 曾潔心 as the hero of the story. Instead of a generic gallery template, we built an indexed archive that makes material research legible: titles, years, process writing and installation images sit in one bilingual system. Email and Instagram stay one tap away, so interest converts into conversation — for tutors, curators, pop-up hosts and future residencies.",
        "features": [
          "Split archive: numbered works list + live media stage",
          "Bilingual artist identity (EN / 中文) from the first viewport",
          "Project pages with process writing and image sequences",
          "About as a living studio statement, not a static bio block",
          "Direct enquiry paths: Email + Instagram CTAs",
          "Mobile-first index for fast scanning at shows and studio visits",
          "Image-heavy Next.js delivery tuned for portfolio performance"
        ],
        "outcomes": [
          "20+ works (2020–2026) organised as a navigable archive",
          "Degree show, Dilston residency and pop-ups documented as chapters",
          "Clear bilingual brand surface for international discovery",
          "A durable home for process — not only finished installation shots"
        ],
